auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

docs {
  # Backend Template

  Click-through collection for the OIDC User Identity microservice — no curl, no
  hand-written JSON. Requests default to Bearer auth using the collection variable
  `access_token`; get one from `oidc/2. Exchange Code for Token`.

  ## Quickstart

  1. Select the **Local** environment (top-right dropdown).
  2. `auth/Register` — creates a user, grab `user_id` from the response.
  3. `oidc/1. Get Login Code (Hydra)` — open its URL (see the request's Docs tab) in a
     real browser tab, log in with the user from step 2, approve consent, copy the
     `code` query param from the final redirect URL.
  4. `oidc/2. Exchange Code for Token` — paste that code into `code` in the request
     body, hit Send. Its post-response script stores `access_token` as a collection
     variable automatically — every other request below picks it up.
  5. `users/Get Me`, `sessions/*`, `2fa/*` now work out of the box.
  6. For `admin/*` (roles/permissions/OAuth clients): set `INITIAL_ADMIN_USER_ID` in
     `.env` to the `user_id` from step 2, then `docker compose up -d --force-recreate api`
     to grant that user the admin role, then repeat steps 3–4 to get a token for that
     admin user.
}
